BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. The Village of Dawn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (     possessed the Spring of Silver, which flowed with clear water but yielded no crops. The Vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    lage of Dusk had rich soil but no water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  For generations, they suffered separately, each guarding their treasure in fear.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  One year, a terrible drought struck. A young farmer from Dawn approached the edge of the valle) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    y, carrying a single precious jar of water. With trembling hands, she poured it onto Dusk's ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    parched earth and retreated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  The people of Dusk watched in wonder. The water sank deep into their blessed soil, and by morn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    ing, three times the amount had bubbled up as a new spring, enriched with minerals from the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    earth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  Grateful, they filled their baskets with the finest grain their soil could produce and carried) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (     them to Dawn. The people of Dawn shared their water again, and again it returned threefold ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    through the earth.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  Soon a river formed between them, flowing both ways according to need. Both villages flourishe) Tj ET
